"Concrete Damage - Uniaxial Scalar Damaged Elasticity (CDP-type)
'<hr />
'<h3>Model</h3>
'Uniaxial <b>damaged elasticity</b>: the stress is the elastic stress
'scaled by a scalar damage variable <var>d</var> that grows during softening:
#math 360 44
\sigma(\varepsilon) = \bigl(1 - d(\varepsilon)\bigr)\,E\,\varepsilon,\qquad d \in [0,1]
#end math
'Sign convention: tension <var>ε</var> &gt; 0 (positive), compression <var>ε</var> &lt; 0.

'<h3>Material properties</h3>
'<table><tr><td>
'Elastic modulus -'E = 30000
'Compressive strength -'f_c = 30
'Peak compressive strain -'ε_c0 = 0.002
'Ultimate compressive strain -'ε_cu = 0.0035
'Tensile strength -'f_t = 3
'Tensile cracking strain -'ε_t0 = f_t/E
'Tension softening strain -'ε_tf = 0.0005
'</td></tr></table>
'Compression softening slope (residual 0.2·f_c reached at ε_cu):
Z = (1 - 0.2)/(ε_cu - ε_c0)

#hide
'--- Constitutive law σ(ε) [MPa] as a function of strain ε ---
'Tension branch: elastic up to ε_t0, then exponential softening
σ_t(ε) = if(ε ≤ ε_t0; E*ε; f_t*exp(-(ε - ε_t0)/ε_tf))
'Compression branch (x = -ε is the magnitude): Hognestad/Kent-Park parabola
'up to the peak, then a linear descending branch with residual 0.2·f_c
σ_c(ε) = if(-ε ≤ ε_c0; -f_c*(2*(-ε/ε_c0) - (-ε/ε_c0)^2); -f_c*max(0.2; 1 - Z*(-ε - ε_c0)))
'Full law by sign of ε
σ(ε) = if(ε ≥ 0; σ_t(ε); σ_c(ε))
'Scalar damage: d = clamp(1 - σ/(E·ε), 0, 1), with d = 0 at ε = 0
d(ε) = if(ε ≡ 0; 0; min(1; max(0; 1 - σ(ε)/(E*ε))))
#show

'<h3>Peak values</h3>
'Compression peak (at ε = -ε_c0): -'σ_peak_c = σ(-ε_c0)' MPa, damage -'d(-ε_c0)
'Tension peak (at ε = +ε_t0): -'σ_peak_t = σ(ε_t0)' MPa, damage -'d(ε_t0)

"Strain sweep with a loop (builds σ and d vectors)
'A #for loop sweeps ε from -0.0035 to +0.0006 and evaluates the engine
'at every point, storing the constitutive response in vectors.
N = 200
ε_ini = -0.0035
ε_fin = 0.0006
Δε = (ε_fin - ε_ini)/(N - 1)
εv = vector(N)
σv = vector(N)
dv = vector(N)
#hide
#for i = 1 : N
    εv.i = ε_ini + (i - 1)*Δε
    σv.i = σ(εv.i)
    dv.i = d(εv.i)
#loop
#show
'Peak compressive stress found by the loop -'min(σv)' MPa
'Maximum damage found by the loop -'max(dv)

"Reference table (validated)
'<table style="border-collapse:collapse" border="1" cellpadding="4">
'<tr><th>ε</th><th>σ (MPa)</th><th>d</th></tr>
'<tr><td>+0.00010</td><td>'σ(0.0001)'</td><td>'d(0.0001)'</td></tr>
'<tr><td>+0.00030</td><td>'σ(0.0003)'</td><td>'d(0.0003)'</td></tr>
'<tr><td>+0.00100</td><td>'σ(0.001)'</td><td>'d(0.001)'</td></tr>
'<tr><td>-0.00100</td><td>'σ(-0.001)'</td><td>'d(-0.001)'</td></tr>
'<tr><td>-0.00200</td><td>'σ(-0.002)'</td><td>'d(-0.002)'</td></tr>
'<tr><td>-0.00300</td><td>'σ(-0.003)'</td><td>'d(-0.003)'</td></tr>
'<tr><td>-0.00350</td><td>'σ(-0.0035)'</td><td>'d(-0.0035)'</td></tr>
'</table>

PlotWidth = 500
PlotHeight = 300
#post
"Constitutive curve  σ(ε)
'Stress-strain law with tensile cracking and compressive softening.
$Plot{εv.k | σv.k @ k = 1 : N}
"Damage evolution  d(ε)
'Scalar damage grows from 0 (undamaged) towards 1 (fully damaged).
$Plot{εv.k | dv.k @ k = 1 : N}
